            or \$A{\textbackslash}in]a,b[=B\$} . The package attempts to solve this using:\\- \texttt{{\textbackslash}interval{\textbraceleft}a{\textbraceright}{\textbraceleft}b{\textbraceright}} -\&gt; \texttt{[a,b]} \\- \texttt{{\textbackslash}interval[open]{\textbraceleft}a{\textbraceright}{\textbraceleft}b{\textbraceright}} -\&gt; \texttt{]a,b[} \\- \texttt{{\textbackslash}interval[open 
            left]{\textbraceleft}a{\textbraceright}{\textbraceleft}b{\textbraceright}} -\&gt; \texttt{]a,b]} 

            The package also supports fence scaling and ensures that the enclosing fences will end up having the 
            proper closing and opening types. TeX maths does not do this job properly.

