userc     = {https://ctan.org/tex-archive/support/make-paper-tarball},
abstract  = {(no language specified) \texttt{make-paper-tarball} is a script that prepares an academic paper manuscript for submission. 
            It performs the following tasks:

            \begin{itemize}
            \item Check that the manuscript can be compiled.
            \item Identify source files (e.g. figures, bibliography) and copy them to a temporary directory.
            \item Rename graphic files after the number of the figure/table that includes them, e.g.  \texttt{figure-1.png} .
            \item Check that figures and tables are cited in order.
            \item Insert LaTeX files included by  \texttt{{\textbackslash}input} directly into the main LaTeX file.
            \item Insert code listings included by  \texttt{{\textbackslash}lstinputlisting} directly into the main LaTeX file.
            \item Insert BibTeX-generated bibliography directly into the main LaTeX file.
            \item Strip out comments.
            \item Copy auxiliary files to the tarball.
            \item Create an archive containing only the the main LaTeX file, required source files, and specified auxiliary files.
            \end{itemize}},
